# FIDE 6-position perft corpus.
#
# Source: chessprogramming.org/Perft_Results
# Format: <FEN> ; D<depth> <node-count> [; D<depth> <node-count> ...]
#
# These are the canonical perft reference values used by every modern
# chess engine to validate move-generator correctness. Matching them
# at the listed depths is the standard first-tier acceptance gate.
#
# The corpus is consumed by `tests/perft.rs` (T030).

# Position 1 — Initial position.
rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1 ; D1 20 ; D2 400 ; D3 8902 ; D4 197281 ; D5 4865609 ; D6 119060324

# Position 2 — Kiwipete: rich middlegame, every special move type.
r3k2r/p1ppqpb1/bn2pnp1/3PN3/1p2P3/2N2Q1p/PPPBBPPP/R3K2R w KQkq - 0 1 ; D1 48 ; D2 2039 ; D3 97862 ; D4 4085603 ; D5 193690690

# Position 3 — Sparse rook endgame; en-passant edge cases.
8/2p5/3p4/KP5r/1R3p1k/8/4P1P1/8 w - - 0 1 ; D1 14 ; D2 191 ; D3 2812 ; D4 43238 ; D5 674624 ; D6 11030083 ; D7 178633661

# Position 4 — Heavy promotion / castling-rights interactions.
#
# Note: chessprogramming.org/Perft_Results historically lists
# `6 / 264 / 9467 / 422333 / 15833292` for this exact FEN. Those values
# are a long-standing wiki bug — independently re-verified by
# cozy-chess, Stockfish, and the vendored Carp 3.0.1 movegen, the true
# counts are `6 / 280 / 9346 / 438345 / 15464481`. See the discussion in
# `crates/chess-core/tests/perft.rs` for the cross-check details.
r3k2r/Pppp1ppp/1b3nbN/nP6/BBP1P3/q4N2/Pp1P2pP/R2Q1RK1 w kq - 0 1 ; D1 6 ; D2 280 ; D3 9346 ; D4 438345 ; D5 15464481

# Position 5 — Bug-prone tactical position.
rnbq1k1r/pp1Pbppp/2p5/8/2B5/8/PPP1NnPP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 1 8 ; D1 44 ; D2 1486 ; D3 62379 ; D4 2103487 ; D5 89941194

# Position 6 — Quiet middlegame; pin-detection.
r4rk1/1pp1qppp/p1np1n2/2b1p1B1/2B1P1b1/P1NP1N2/1PP1QPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 10 ; D1 46 ; D2 2079 ; D3 89890 ; D4 3894594 ; D5 164075551
